  'No. The virtual work visa permits residency in the UAE while working exclusively for employers or clients outside the country. Working for UAE-based entities requires a different visa and a MoHRE work permit. Freelancers seeking to serve UAE clients should consider a freelance permit or business licence.': 'No. The virtual work visa permits residency in the UAE while working exclusively for employers or clients outside the country. Working for UAE-based entities requires a different visa and a MoHRE work permit. Freelancers seeking to serve UAE clients should consider a freelance permit or business licence.',
  'No. Under standard UAE immigration law, expatriates must sponsor both parents together. Sponsoring a single parent is only permitted on strict humanitarian grounds with attested legal proof that one parent is deceased (death certificate) or that parents are legally divorced with custody judgment, or if the sponsor is an only child.': 'No. Under standard UAE immigration law, expatriates must sponsor both parents together. Sponsoring a single parent is only permitted on strict humanitarian grounds with attested legal proof that one parent is deceased (death certificate) or that parents are legally divorced with custody judgment, or if the sponsor is an only child.',
