  'Travellers use both phrases. “Dubai visa” reflects the destination people search for; “UAE visa” describes the country-level entry permission. An approved UAE tourist visa generally allows eligible travellers to visit Dubai, Abu Dhabi, Sharjah, Ajman, Umm Al Quwain, Ras Al Khaimah and Fujairah, subject to the conditions of the issued visa.': 'Travellers use both phrases. “Dubai visa” reflects the destination people search for; “UAE visa” describes the country-level entry permission. An approved UAE tourist visa generally allows eligible travellers to visit Dubai, Abu Dhabi, Sharjah, Ajman, Umm Al Quwain, Ras Al Khaimah and Fujairah, subject to the conditions of the issued visa.',
